# Master-plan 600-900px notes-cell full-width fix (user-reported tablet screenshot, 2026-09-09)

## Scope
frontend/src/features/dispatch/master-plan/MasterPlanGrid.css + its contract test.
Pure CSS layout fix; no JSX / TS / schema / API changes.

## Bug
At container widths 600-900px (tablet band), the action cell (Phân bổ nhà xe, cell 7) was
forced full-width via `.master-plan-grid__cell--action { grid-column: 1 / -1 }`, but cell 8
(Ghi chú) was not spanned. In a 2-col CSS grid, after the full-width action cell, cell 8
auto-flowed into the next row's LEFT column alone — leaving the right half empty and
drawing a half-width border-top from `:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }`.

The ≤599px band already handled this with `:nth-child(8) { grid-column: 1 / -1 }`. The
600-900px band missed it.

## Fix
Mirror the ≤599px rule into the 600-900px band:

```css
.master-plan-grid__cell:nth-child(8) {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  border-inline-start: 0;
}
```

`border-inline-start: 0` drops the inline-start that `:nth-child(even)` would otherwise
apply, so the spanned cell doesn't double the card's left edge.

