After pushing 5324b1ad + 989e1e0b (caught the deploy gap thanks to QA #166),
folded the visual polish on top in the same wave per PM's "no extra deploys" rule:

- 9376ac1b — style(dispatch): ground the master-plan notes cell to the 44px
  touch floor.

Rationale: in the @container (max-width: 900px) card view, the action cell holds a
44px trigger (~64px cell body). The notes cell below it was rendering at its natural
text height (~40-50px) — 14-24px height pop in the footer pair. Pinning
`.master-plan-grid__notes-trigger { min-height: 44px }` inside the ≤900px card view
grounds empty/short notes to the action-cell rhythm AND keeps the 44px touch target
that design-system.md reserves for tappable surfaces. Desktop table view untouched.

